---
import ChapterLayout from '../../../layouts/ChapterLayout.astro';
import { getDrakeChapter } from '../../../data/story/drakeChaptersData';
import { processDrakeContentHtml } from '../../../utils/drakeContentProcessor';

const chapter = getDrakeChapter('013-light', 'epilogue-part-1')!;

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;

const rawContentHtml = "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Part 20 - the time to end Light to All and bring this cycle to a close is upon us!\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Preparations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Preparations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#A_Light_in_the_Darkness\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">A Light in the Darkness</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Clipping_An_Angel&#39;s_Wings\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Clipping An Angel's Wings</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Cruel_Truths\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Cruel Truths</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Beauty_Ne&#39;er_Tarnished\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Beauty Ne'er Tarnished</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Preparations\">Preparations</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Preparations\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_20?action=edit&amp;section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Preparations\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the Epilogue you can use whatever party of 5 you like, and in each gateway your Assist will be randomly chosen from the five people you left out. You can use whoever you like, I took a part of Zidane, Terra, Cloud, Firion and Squall. I bought all of them two more accessory slots, for a total of 8, and that Sunrise is finally gone, we need no more Battlegen until certain gateways in Confessions of the Creator. The line-up for them all is a Power Ring, Hyper Ring, Muscle Belt (Earring for Terra, obviously), HP = 100%, BRV ≥ Base Value, Summpon Unused, (Opp) Break, and Level 10-19. The Power Ring is back because I have no worthwhile 1.3x boosters, and a 1.2x boost to 12% is less than a flat 3% boost. I bought Zidane an extra accessory slot to give him the Rabbit's Foot so Cactuar recharges faster, just in case.\n</p><p>Double-check everyone's equipment, the characters from the earlier storylines may be outdated. During the storyline we'll hit Level 30 and we'll cover the equipment I know you've all been waiting for. Also check abilities in case anyone learned new ones in the final battles of their storylines, a few did for me. When entering each gateway in this storyline, remember your Assist is random - if you get one you don't like, just exit the gateway and re-enter. Everyone save for the Warrior of Light is level 15 or 16, but the bonus line is 23, odd. Still no exp bonuses for us, I don't want to dilute the difficulty by being overleveled - not that the difficulty has been very high anyway, right?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"A_Light_in_the_Darkness\">A Light in the Darkness</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: A Light in the Darkness\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_20?action=edit&amp;section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: A Light in the Darkness\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>With Cosmos dead, the ten warriors fade away one by one, Kefka taunting it's their fault she was killed. As they fall into darkness however, the Crystals light up the area and they find themselves back in Order's Sanctuary. They're on borrowed time, but they have to track down the Chaos Warriors, find out what happened to Cosmos, and take out Chaos!\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">I\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"28000 gil\"><img alt=\"28000 gil\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><b>AC</b>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Booster Accessory multiplier 5x\"><img alt=\"Booster Accessory multiplier 5x\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Blue.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Blue.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20121006224522\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Party Battle\"><img alt=\"Party Battle\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"30\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Party Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/30?cb=20121006224522\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Exdeath\"><img alt=\"Exdeath\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"><img alt=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Phantom\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Phantom\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As you should be used to, there are gonna be Party pieces to contend with in the epilogue. To refresh your memory, in Tournament the party leaders fight, whoever dies is replaced with the next person in line, and so on until one party is entirely beaten. Round-Robin, party leaders fight, then second in line fight, until one party has the majority win (two wins against a three-enemy party). I'll be using Round Robin for all my fights, but if you like Tournament you can use Tournament. The KP Chance is a 90 second win, and there's no way to chain all enemies here so beat the Party piece and ignore the last two, it's a waste of a chain skill to get the two of them. The blue emblem is a booster x5, always welcome.\n</p><p>As we enter battle, we get notified of the Omega arenas. All arenas in this last chapter are the Omega versions, I'll explain what they do as they come up. The first foe is a Fallacious Tree with Sword Dance and Hurricane. He's fought in World of Darkness Ω, here wisps of darkness appear to signal an arena shift, if you're near the opponent the arena becomes a very small closed-in room dominated by pillars, if you're far away the arena becomes a huge-wide open arena of platforms connected by grind bars. In both, the Bravery pool rises rapidly depending on distance, in the close arena it rises faster the closer you are, and vice-versa for the open arena. \n</p><p>Second is a Delusory Warlock with Rising Wave, Gravity System, Nightglow, the Magus Sisters summon to halve your Bravery when you Break him and a Hyper Ring with 8 HP = 100% 1.5x boosters, and a No BRV Damage 3x booster. Naturally priority goes to turning them off fast. Contrary to previous chapters, enemies switch up accessories throughout the journey rather than all of them using one set-up. The Warlock is fought in Lunar Subterrane Ω, pretty lame gimmick, the cliffs now boost the stage Bravery when destroyed. The last foe is an Imaginary Champion with Godspeed, Shadow Flare, Black Materia, Shiva for a summon, the Hyper Ring set-up, and is fought in Empyreal Paradox Ω. Here there are wisps of light near the Crystal that slowly drain the Bravery of nearby fighters and transfer the drained Bravery to the stage pool. Quite helpful in Confessions of the Creator since it helps you whittle down the Bravery of high-level foes.\n</p><p>The last two enemies, if you must fight them, are a Counterfeit Wraith in the Empyreal Paradox with Tentacle of Spite (large energy orb blast), Anti-Air Particle Beam, the Hyper Ring stuff, and Ultros. The other is an Ephmeral Phantom with Jecht Rush, Jecht Block, and is fought in Chaos Shrine Ω. Here, both characters are regularly drained of a percentage of their Bravery and have it added to the Bravery pool.\n</p><p>The chest has 28,000 gil.\n</p><p>As we leave, Exdeath confronts us and explains the truth of why Cosmos was killed, a truth we already know from the 12th cycle - the Crystals are fragments of Cosmos's power, and to obtain them was to deprive her of that power. We've only survived because her power is in those Crystals still, but it won't last long. Now of course comes the inevitable fight. I won't do boss templates this time, you can see the boss's stats for yourself, I'll note moves and summon and such in text.\n</p><p>Exdeath is a tough cookie, Level 26 with Level 30 equipment, an Earring connected to 6 Near Opponent boosters (hello Hurricane, OW THAT HURTS!), and a new accessory to us, Prayer Beads, which will sap our critical hit chances. He has a Fallacious Wanderer Assist, Tiamat as a summon, and the typical tricks for his moveset, Reverse Polarity, Black Hole, Hurricane, Turn Guard, Omni Block, Malestrom, Delta Attack and Almagest. And we're fighting on The Rift Ω, one of the coolest Omega arenas. As you can see everything is topsy-turvy, turrets stacked on each other and spires floating in the air. Periodically the castle features will rearrange themselves in new ways, increasing the Bravery pool during the process. Be sure to grab any EX Cores as they appear because they may vanish during the shake-up.\n</p><p>Because he is so predictable and you know how to bait him, this fight isn't hard, just long, he has high defenses and a lot of Bravery and HP to whittle down. Attack when he isn't nearby to charge up your Assist and perform combo attacks to up the damage output, and remember to use your summon if needed. Overall it'll take time to put him down due to his power levels exceeding any prior opponent, but you'll prevail in the end. \n</p><p>Exdeath fades away for good now, laughing, and the warriors wonder why Cosmos would have them get the Crystals if it meant her destruction. They decide she must have known she was going to be destroyed and gave them her power as a last hope, so let's not waste it. Also fun note, the scenes before and after the Exdeath fight, along with two others, change depending on who the party leader is.\n</p><p>We unlock a new Report now, if you want to go watch, no fights though so I won't cover it. While I checked though I swung by Chapter 5 in the 012 story to visit the moogle who sells rare items, and bought a KP Bonus. If you kiddies can go buy one, it depends on your bonus day, do so. I'll be saving this for later, mwa ha ha! I also brought the Pre-EX Mode booster. It remains active as long as you haven't used EX Mode during the fight and is a nice 1.4x booster, so it replaced the Power Ring on my party members. There are other ones including Pre-Air Dash and Pre-EX Revenge, guess how they work, but they're 200 KP each and I could only afford one.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Clipping_An_Angel.27s_Wings\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Clipping_An_Angel's_Wings\">Clipping An Angel's Wings</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Clipping An Angel&#39;s Wings\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_20?action=edit&amp;section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Clipping An Angel&#39;s Wings\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On the world map now, we're in a new end of the Land of Discord, behind us is a long, empty beach. Moving ahead there's a chest with 20,000 gil, and to the right a moogle and a chest with a BRV Charge. The moogle sells trade accessories we don't need anymore, you found a lot of them in the storylines up to this point. Buy a Multichain and a Straight Chain. Approach the blue gateway. Cloud senses Sephiroth inside, so let's go say hello. A warning, once you enter the gateway, the only way out is through Sephiroth, you can exit the gateway as you can with all of them but you won't get KP.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Epitaph Stone\"><img alt=\"Epitaph Stone\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204003912\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"False Stalwart\"><img alt=\"False Stalwart\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"25\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Expert Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/25?cb=20110204003912\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/fc/DFF_Potion.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235732\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Potion\"><img alt=\"Potion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"21\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Potion.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Potion.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/fc/DFF_Potion.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/21?cb=20110203235732\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Imaginary Champion\"><img alt=\"Imaginary Champion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Sephiroth\"><img alt=\"Sephiroth\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><b>AC</b>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Magic Critical Rate Up\"><img alt=\"Magic Critical Rate Up\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Blue.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Blue.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Initial Stage BRV Boost\"><img alt=\"Initial Stage BRV Boost\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Delusory Dragoon\"><img alt=\"Delusory Dragoon\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Straight Chain at B7, of course. True there's only three but a Straight Chain is 8 KP and we'll win 9 for the three chain, so it's a slight profit, right? The KP Chance is a 90 second win. The emblem is a magical critical rate up, so if you brought Terra along - and why the hell didn't you if not? - consider swapping her in to take advantage of it. Otherwise Zidane's Meo Twister, Tidus's Energy Rain, and everyone else's usual spells will appreciate the benefits. Don't worry about being hurt, there's a Potion for us before we leave and confront Sephy.\n</p><p>First comes an Imaginary Champion with the Moogle summon, a Hyper Ring and 9 Near Loss boosters, that's gonna suck when they go off. He uses Shadow Flare, Fervent Blow and Godspeed. Next is the Strange enemy, a Delusory Dragoon, it begins with a lot of Bravery, spams Jump, and has Cactuar, an easy victory. The Expert piece is a False Stalwart with two Muscle Belts, six Near Opponent, an after 45 Seconds, and the Cactuar summon. For his moveset he has Twist Drill, Twin Swords, Bardiche, Blaze, and Flare. He's fought in Dream's End Ω, the Bravery pool will skyrocket here as every attack, successful or not, will drive up the Bravery pool. He's pretty tough but you can handle him, he's oddly not as smart as I've come to expect from Expert enemies. \n</p><p>The chest has an Epitaph Stone, which is needed for some level 30 and 60 gear. I also became able to buy the accessories for such in the shop by trading in Elixirs, but we don't need any right yet.\n</p><p>A nice change between Dissidia and D012 was that in Shade Impulse, you got a special scene if your character as a villain's rival, for the other villains aside from Exdeath, the Emperor and Garland, you just got a couple text boxes. D012 includes all the scenes, so even if Cloud isn't your party leader, or not in the party at all, you'll see this scene when you leave. Sephiroth does what he does best - spout cryptic meaningless Ho Yay babble about how Cloud clings to him out of despair because he holds onto hope that's eating him like a disease. Cloud will just have to endure it then. And of course now it's fight time, sorry Cloud, you can square off but this is Zidane's show.\n</p><p>Sephiroth too has level 30 equipment, he has a significantly greater attack strength than Exdeath, but significantly lower defenses. He's got over 4,200 HP and a Muscle Belt hooked up to 6 Attacking Bravery boosters, ouch. He has the Alexander summon and an Imaginary Soldier Assist. His moveset is the usual - Reaper, Fervent Blow, Transience, Oblivion, Godspeed, Shadow Flare. For HP attacks, Hell's Gate, Octaslash, Scintilla - I didn't see them but assume Black Materia and Heaven's Light are there too. The stage, Planet's Core Ω, is one of two stages that I consider the worst in the game. After a period of time the stage will shake and shift form. The floating rocks vanish and more tendrils of lifestream to quickmove on appear. The only platforms now aside from the large central one at the bottom are a handful of floating pillars that crumble when dashed into - and of course EX Cores will appear on top of them and vanish when you dash into the pillar trying to get to them. This is annoying enough, the lack of solid ground, but what makes the stage terrible is the AI <i>loves</i> to quickmove along the grindbars and up the walls endlessly for no reason, forcing you to track them down. You'll see soon enough. For a fun twist though, try going into an EX Burst during the stage shift, the EX Burst background will be lit up!\n</p><p>Sephiroth is overall a pushover, he has a heavy defense penalty compared to Exdeath and Zidane quickly sapped his HP away with his Tempest and Swift Attack HP links.  True his own damage output is also pretty impressive, but you know how (not) aggressive the AI is, and it won't take advantage of this. As for damage output - Zidane's EX Burst did 1000 damage, plus the Bravery pool was higher due to the stage shifting. All in all, once you get Sephiroth to half HP, as long as his Bravery isn't in Break status so you can re-Break him, an EX Burst can kill him. Beaten, Sephiroth stands up...somehow in front of Cloud again, and declares he doesn't exist...okay. Cloud rejects his taunts again and Sephiroth claims his shadow is burned into Cloud's heart and that they will meet again. Did a yaoi fangirl write this dialogue?\n</p><p>On the world map again, go right to find a Maser Eye and another blue gateway with treasure. Save the Maser Eye, we'll have use for it later.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decodin