lor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"><img alt=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Magic Critical Rate Up\"><img alt=\"Magic Critical Rate Up\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Blue.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Blue.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><b>AC</b>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204003912\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Imitation Despot\"><img alt=\"Imitation Despot\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"25\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Expert Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/25?cb=20110204003912\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"><img alt=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Polished Ore\"><img alt=\"Polished Ore\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Multichain at C3 to get all four enemies. I swapped Terra in as party leader for this and the next gateway. The emblem is a magical critical rate up, Terra likes that of course. The KP Chance is a 90 second win, and there's another Expert enemy so let's fill that EX Gauge! Also note my party is outgrowing the Level 10-19 booster, replace it with a Power Ring when that occurs since Level 20-29 is only a 1.2 booster.\n</p><p>The first enemy is a Counterfeit Wraith with Tentacle of Suffering (aerial spin attack), she's fought in Crystal World Ω. Here platforms of crystal appear in the air, and the Bravery pool rises each time. Destroying the crystal platforms causes more to appear in new formations, in turn raising the Bravery pool again. The second enemy is a Phantasmal Harlequin with the two Firaga attacks, Hyperdrive, Moogle summon, and a Hyper Ring with 9 Near Loss. Next is an Idle Sky Pirate with high initial Bravery, the Moogle summon, and Windburst. \n</p><p>The Expert enemy is an Imitation Despot with the usual moveset, two Earrings with six Far From Opponent, and an after 45 Seconds. He has a Phantasmal Harlequin for an Assist and Carbuncle for a summon. He'll use Carbuncle when low on Bravery so your Break won't give you as much as we'd like, but otherwise you know how to handle him, the Chaos Shrine is a wide open area so his traps won't work well here. Try to Break him all at once so he can't get Carbuncle off.\n</p><p>With the enemies beaten, take the Polished Ore from the chest and leave.\n</p><p>On the overworld again head to the shoreline to find a rock to break to reach an island with a Gargoyle Pebble. Now just the next gateway.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Cruel_Truths\">Cruel Truths</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Cruel Truths\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_20?action=edit&amp;section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Cruel Truths\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As we enter, the Emperor appears before us. The party is surprised to see him alive since they thought Firion beat him. How could anyone tell, the villains almost always fade away when beaten but yet they come back for more later. The Emperor is looking to rule this world, and declares that with Chaos's victory, the Warriors of Chaos are free to pursue their own desires outside the war. He vanishes with a laughing, and the Warriors continue on.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Initial Stage BRV Boost\"><img alt=\"Initial Stage BRV Boost\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20121006224522\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Party Battle\"><img alt=\"Party Battle\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"30\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Party Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/30?cb=20121006224522\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"29000 gil\"><img alt=\"29000 gil\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Kefka Palazzo\"><img alt=\"Kefka Palazzo\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><b>AC</b>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Lizardman Skin\"><img alt=\"Lizardman Skin\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20121006224522\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Party Battle\"><img alt=\"Party Battle\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"30\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Party Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/30?cb=20121006224522\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>There's any number of ways to get both Party pieces. A Round Chain or Cross Chain can do it at D5, missing the emblem, while a Straight Chain or Multichain at D4 can use the emblem. It depends on what you have I used a Round Chain since it's cheaper/easier to replace. There are six enemies here, but the KP Gambler should still be saved. The bonus line is 28 - HA! - and the KP Chance is a 60 second Break.\n</p><p>First is a Transient Witch with Knight's Blade, Knight's Arrow, Great Attractor, the Carbuncle summon, and the accessory gimmick of this gateway, it should seem familiar - a Zephyr Cloak, Heart's Ease, Iifa Dew, and 7 Near Loss, giving them a Bravery boost whenever they block or dodge an attack once you have enough Bravery to kill them. The Dew is different from the Leaf, you don't survive with 1 HP, your Bravery drains to 0 and you get as much HP as Bravery lost. It doesn't work if they're in Break though, keep that in mind. Next comes a Phantasmal Harlequin with the same accessories, Havoc Wing, and Demon Wall. The third foe, which you don't have to fight in Round Robin, is a Capricious Reaper with Seraphic Star and those accessories again\n</p><p>The second Party piece begins simply with a Capricious Reaper with Seraphic Star and nothing else. Second is a Transient Witch with Shockwave Pulsar. The last one, which again you don't have to fight if you use Round Robin, is a False Stalwart with Twin Swords, Magus Sisters, and the Iifa Dew set-up.\n</p><p>With 36 KP in our pocket, open up the chests for Lizardman Skin and 29,000 gil. At the end, Terra finds Kefka and demands answers from him, but Kefka, being Kefka just taunts her and laughs that at this point it doesn't matter and attacks.\n</p><p>Kefka doesn't have quite as much attack strength as Sephiroth, but has higher defense. He's got an Earring with 6 Far From Opponent, ouch, a Bomb for a summon and a Phantasmal Girl Assist. His moveset is the two Thundaga attacks, Scatter-Spray Blizzaga, Extra-Crispy Firaga, and Meteor, with all his HP hits. The stage is Kefka's Tower Ω, here every time a part of the stage is destroyed, \"magitek steam\" will blast out of the walls in the lower parts of the factory, damaging the Bravery of fighters that are hit and increasing the Bravery pool. This can also occur when wall rushing them in the lower parts, and can lead to a very amusing \"pinball\" effect of knocking them into a wall and then they bounce back and forth for a second between vents of steam.\n</p><p>Kefka's attacks pack a serious wallop, even without those boosters activated, and are always tricky to avoid, especially Scatter-Spray Blizzaga. However, as you may remember from her chapter in her EX Mode Terra becomes a goddess of magical carnage, and entering battle with a full EX Gauge I had little trouble taking Kefka down with her power boost - just remember to enter Chases to keep the gauge filled! In the aftermath of the fight, Kefka is still yearning for destruction, and laments that hope and dreams aren't enough to make a fulfilling life, and explodes in a sad laugh as he calls out for yet more destruction. Terra wonders if that was why Kefka destroyed, and continues on.\n</p><p>Now we get an interlude scene of Garland confronting Golbez on his hand in the events that have unfolded, revealing that the cycles were to go on forever to temper Chaos into a perfect weapon of destruction. Golbez, stunned, asks Garland just who he is.\n</p><p>We also unlock another Report, with no battles so as I said I won't cover it.\n</p><p>Back on the world map, Cloud is gonna be the party leader for the next couple of gateways. I also swapped Firion and Squall up to the second and third slots, as they haven't been getting Exp from Party pieces and so they and Cloud are a few levels behind Zidane and Terra. Plus it helps keep things fresh, and while the non-fighters get exp, they don't get AP, so let's spread the love.\n</p><p>Goi around the beach to where the teleport stone used to be, the chest has a Treant Branch. Shatter the rock and grind over to find a Silver Lobo Claw. As a note, the party members here will note the lack of enemies outside the gateways, wondering if the destruction of the world has destroyed them, and note the teleport stone is gone. Approach the blue gateway and Onion Knight will sense an old friend inside. If you need a Straight Chain, go back and grab one from the moogle, and grab a Cross Chain while you're over there too.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Wererat Claw\"><img alt=\"Wererat Claw\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Capricious Reaper\"><img alt=\"Capricious Reaper\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><b>AC</b>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Capricious Reaper\"><img alt=\"Capricious Reaper\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Initial BRV Boost for both\"><img alt=\"Initial BRV Boost for both\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Gunner\"><img alt=\"Transient Gunner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Cloud of Darkness\"><img alt=\"Cloud of Darkness\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20121006224522\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Party Battle\"><img alt=\"Party Battle\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"30\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Party Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/30?cb=20121006224522\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>No way to get all of them at once, but a Straight Chain at C4 will do it, it's an Initial BRV Boost emblem and as a purple one will benefit the enemy too, make sure your summons are equipped if you need help draining their Bravery. The KP Chance is a 90 second win, easy to get, you won't even need to Break enemies to beat them quickly thanks to the emblem.\n</p><p>The Normal enemy is a humble, wimpy, Capricious Reaper with Snatch Shot and Burst Energy. The Hard enemy is a second Reaper with Snatch Shot, Flare Star, an unknown Assist and summon, and another familiar line of accessories - Arcane Resin, Muscle Belt, Earring, Attractorb, Pearl Necklace, and 5 EX Mode boosters. Enjoy your enemy being in EX Mode for most of the fight and having a nice damage buff for it! The Strange enemy has a similar accessory build, an Arcane Resin with a Muscle Belt, Hyper Ring and 5 Near Opponent, along with 1 HP of course, and the Moogle summon. His moveset is Machine Gun and Ragnarok Blade.\n</p><p>The Party piece, first is a False Stalwart with Round Edge and Twin Swords. Second is a Delusory Warlock with Rising Wave, Float System, Genesis Rock, the Reaper's EX Mode stuff, and the Moogle summon. The last foe is an Ephemeral Phantom with the same accessories, but that's all I know, I didn't have to actually fight him and neither do you.\n</p><p>The chest has a Wererat Claw, then approach the end piece. The Onion Knight approaches the Cloud of Darkness, and declares that even if Cosmos is gone, he can still fight to uphold her last hope, and of course fight time.\n</p><p>The Cloud of Darkness is actually only slightly stronger than Exdeath, with a lower level and attack and defense on par or worse than Kefka's. Her accessories are decent, a Pearl Necklace and an Attractorb Orb with the 15, 30, 45, 60 and 90 Second boosters, one each. She has the Land Worm summon, all four tentacle attacks, and a few new HP attacks. Feint Particle Beam, only on the ground, has her vanish into a dark portal to dodge attacks then reappear somewhere else to fire an orb of darkness as you, fairly easy to avoid, and Wrath Particle Beam is an aerial move where she blocks and summons an orb of darkness to strike you. It's not impervious to all attacks like Omni Block, but can block anything with lower priority than High, which mostly means any non-HP attacks.\n</p><p>She's pretty simple to beat, unless you find yourself tripped up by her new HP attacks that is. All her Bravery attacks can be blocked and punished, and Land Worm's drain is only a nuisance, as long as you stay close to her it won't do much, and you want to be close so she's more likely to do a Bravery attack and you can block and punish her. And since I was using Cloud, my EX Mode gave me free reign to go nuts on her since all of Cloud's attacks break or stagger her on a conflict between attacks. With the Cloud of Darkness weakened, she tells the Onion Knight that there is no point to trying anymore, but the Onion Knight has to listen to his heart over his head. The Cloud of Darkness fades away into a portal of darkness, returning to her slumber.\n</p><p>On the overworld map again, head down the path to find a chest with an EX Charge, then head into the gateway.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Beauty_Ne.27er_Tarnished\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Beauty_Ne'er_Tarnished\">Beauty Ne'er Tarnished</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Beauty Ne&#39;er Tarnished\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_20?action=edit&amp;section=5\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Beauty Ne&#39;er Tarnished\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As we enter, Garland reveals to Golbez he was a prisoner of a time loop, but the \"Great Will\" freed him and brought him to this realm to orchestrate war between Chaos and Cosmos. Golbez however asks what Garland himself has wished for, since the war is now over he can pursue his own path. Garland cannot accept this \"hope\" and is resigned to enjoying the last final battles.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Kuja\"><img alt=\"Kuja\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20121006224522\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Party Battle\"><img alt=\"Party Battle\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"30\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Party Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/30?cb=20121006224522\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Magic Critical Rate Up\"><img alt=\"Magic Critical Rate Up\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Blue.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Blue.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Scorpion\"><img alt=\"Scorpion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Initial BRV Boost for both\"><img alt=\"Initial BRV Boost for both\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204003912\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"><img alt=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"25\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Expert Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/25?cb=20110204003912\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/f5/D012_Phoenix_Down.png/revision/latest?cb=20120409211126\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Phoenix Down\"><img alt=\"Phoenix Down\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"10\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Phoenix Down.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Phoenix_Down.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/f5/D012_Phoenix_Down.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/10?cb=20120409211126\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><b>AC</b>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Cross Chain at C1 to get all enemies here, the blue emblem is a magic critical rate up, but I'm sticking to Cloud for now so it'll be passed up. The bonus line is 30 and the KP Chance is a 90 second win. Also note bonus line, in all storylines, takes into account the levels of the entire party, and looks at whoever has the highest level among them to determine the starting KP. I used my EX Charge, might as well, three slots are being taken up by a KP Gambler, KP Bonus and Maser Eye. It'll be worth it, kiddies, be patient.\n</p><p>The Strange enemy is first, an Ephemeral Summoner. She has high starting Bravery, summons Tiamat, and spams Thor's Hammer. An easy win, remember to attack through Thor's Hammer with HP attacks like Rough Divide, Straightarrow, Braver, etc. Next is the Expert piece, a Counterfeit Wraith with all four Tentacle attacks, Anti-Air, Fusillade, Wrath and 0-Form Particle Beams, the Ifrit summon, and unknown Assist, and some accessories of course - a Hyper Ring and Guardian Bangle with 8 HP = 100% boosters. The stage is Ultimecia's Castle Ω. Here, regularly Time Compression will occur, randomizing the Bravery pool rapidly, even during an EX Burst, and reforming destroyed stage elements. The gears in the stage also spin rapidly, damaging characters and knocking them around. Cloud's EX Mode helps a lot to deplete the Expert's high Bravery in time to meet the KP Chance.\n</p><p>Now it's Party time of course. First, a wimpy Phantasmal Harlequin with Hyperdrive. Next is an Imitation Despot with Thunder Crest, Light Crest and Flare. He's fought in Pandaemonium Ω, here the two halves of the stage (the pit and hallway separate them) will have their floors turn red and black while the other is normal, then they switch. While fighting over the red and black areas, spikes will pop out at random and stab into the air, knocking characters into the air and damaging their Bravery and adding it to the pool. Spikes can also hit and lock Assists so be cautious calling them in such areas. The grey floors are safe, fortunately. The last enemy I avoided is a False Stalwart with a Hyper Ring hooked up to 4 HP = 100% and 5 BRV ≥ Base Value, and he uses Cyclone.\n</p><p>The chest has a Scorpion, a level 30 weapon we thus cannot use yet.\n</p><p>As we reach the end we come upon Kuja, still spouting off his poetry. Zidane still refuses to give up, and of course there's only one thing to do - let another party member beat the shit out of him.\n</p><p>Kuja's offense is only equal to the Cloud of Darknesses, but he's got the highest defense yet, and as with all previous bosses a few hundred more HP over the last one. His boosters are pretty pathetic though, a Pearl Necklace, Attractorb and Earring with three Aerial boosters, that's only a 3.3x booster, we have more than that! Give him at least five or so. For moves he's got Ring Holy, Remote Flare, Burst Energy, Strike Energy, Snatch Shot, Flare Star, Seraphic Star, Force Symphony, and Ultima - basically, all the moves he's ever had. His summon is Magic Pot and he's got a Capricious Thief Assist. Also, they got it right this time and use the proper boss music they should have had in Chapter 8.\n</p><p>I decided not to use Cloud's EX Mode and fought normally, and since I had no HP links yet, it was a rough ride. Kuja's attacks are always annoying to avoid, especially his HP attacks, and he was good about charging and using his Capricious Thief Assist. Rising Fang was my main offense since Cloud has trouble striking from above and being in front of Kuja is about the worst place you can be. True, being below him is never a good idea...god I can write innuendo so well ;p, but Rising Fang is a decently quick response, even striking Kuja during his Force Symphony conducting. So overall, he's pretty tough without an EX Gauge to help you out. With one? Crush him, Cloud's EX Mode bonus will blast his Bravery into oblivion and can clinch the match by knocking off half his HP with ease.\n</p><p>As Kuja lies dying, he asks Zidane to finish him off, as his inability to understand hope means life itself has defeated him. And yet, Zidane still tries to help him. Kuja cannot understand why and pushes him away, fading away with dignity.\n</p><p>Afterward we see a scene of the Emperor and Jecht. The Emperor tells Jecht that with Cosmos dead, soon Chaos's warriors too will fade, and when Jecht protests, the Emperor tells him he isn't one of Chaos's minions. We also unlock Report 15, with fights this time.\n</p><p>On the overworld map again, it's Firion's turn to lead the posse. Note Bartz has a very intriguing thing to say here if you chat him up. Go along the path to a blue gateway, on the left is a chest with an Assist Charge and further down the path is a chest with a Zu Feather. Now we're heading into the gateway of course, we need a Cross Chain, go all the way back and buy one, and to save a trip get a Multichain too. As we approach the gateway, Squall senses a particular someone inside.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ultimecia\"><img alt=\"Ultimecia\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Imaginary Soldier\"><img alt=\"Imaginary Soldier\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Capricious Thief\"><img alt=\"Capricious Thief\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Lion\"><img alt=\"Transient Lion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><b>AC</b>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Vision\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Vision\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Imaginary Brawler\"><img alt=\"Imaginary Brawler\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Cockatrice Feather\"><img alt=\"Cockatrice Feather\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Cross Chain at E3 to get all five, yup, all five Strange enemies. And they all use different gimmicks. This is gonna be a treat! The KP Chance is a 90 second win, absolute piece of cake, take your time filling up that EX Gauge kiddies.\n</p><p>First is a Capricious Thief, he has an Iifa Leaf and barely enough HP to use it as always, an initial Bravery boost, an Arcane Resin, the Mandragora summon to keep his Bravery regen rate up to insane levels, and he spams Grand Lethal. Keep your distance from him to avoid it and get him as he recovers. Second is an Ephemeral Vision with an Arcane Resin, a Muscle Belt, Hyper Ring, and 5 Near Opponent boosters, with the Moogle summon for random fun, and it likes Wither Shot. Third is an Imaginary Brawler with a Bravery boost, Cactuar, and it likes Blizzara. The fourth foe is an Imaginary Soldier with a <i>huge</i> Bravery boost, Odin, and it likes using Slashing Blow to Omnislash Version 5 HP link. The last enemy is a Transient Lion who likes Fusillade and Beat Fang, he comes into the fight with 0 Bravery and a Guardian Bangle connected to three HP = 1 boosters, and of course, it uses the Carbuncle summon at the start of the fight.\n</p><p>The chest has a Cockatrice Feather.\n</p><p>As we arrive at Ultimecia's lair, Squall asks her what she wants. Ultimecia wants a world of compressed time where Squall will worship her as a god. Squall tells her in no uncertain terms \"get over yourself\", and Ultimecia says he's just the same as hers, trying to create his vision of an ideal world. Squall agrees, and says he has a promise to keep. They then exchange the obligatory taunts before fighting...for...some reason. Well, Squall's entire story was full of mixed messages and confusing morals, why break tradition?\n</p><p>Ultimecia naturally has all previous moves you've dealt with, and a new one, Hell's Judgment, it creates a crest of magic below you and blasts you up into the air. For accessories she's got an Earring with 2 HP = 1, 2 Near Death, 3 Near Loss, and an Iifa Leaf, giving her an impressive boost to damage on the bring of death. She also uses the Marilith summon, has a Transient Lion Assist, and has the high attack power of Kefka and Sephiroth with the high defense of Kuja, giving her the best stats yet.\n</p><p>However, she is, as always, an idiot. At one point with Firion I just spammed Straightarrow - yes she dodged it sometimes, but it also hit far too often, because she would respond by using an attack of her own, making her unable to dodge. I also had great ease catching her with Reel Axe to Bravery pain, and in general she was just really bad at avoiding Firion's attacks. And you've used him, you know it is not difficult to avoid Firion's attacks, <i>especially</i> Straightarrow. Even that aside, I could just camp and use Shield Bash over and over, all of her uncharged attacks - which are mostly all I found her using - trigger it. Also have fun throwing a Reel Axe at her during a charged Knight's Blade, the Axe has higher damage priority and will deflect the blades as it flies towards her. The only complications were Marilith and the Iifa Leaf, but they only work once and are just nuisances.\n</p><p>As Ultimecia stands weakened and vanishing, she philosophizes that time will always slip through your grasp and the happiness of the moment is fleeting - all she wants is to take hold of that. Squall then strikes her down before she can continue, and says he can't let anyone take his time from him. So once again, the game portrays Squall as a callous, self-righteous prick.\n</p><p>On the world map, head to the next gateway, collecting the orbs of the dead and a Shockwave from the chest, a new skill that reduces enemies to half their normal levels in chains.\n</p><p>This part has gotten long kiddies, so I'll see you on the second part and the next page!\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"toccolours\" width=\"85%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; margin:0 auto; text-align: center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: center; border:solid 1px\"><b><a href=\"/story/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake\">Drake Clawfang's Dissidia 012 Walkthrough</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-10/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 19\">Previous page</a></b>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Treachery_of_the_Gods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Treachery of the Gods\">Treachery of the Gods</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/prologue-chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 1\">Prologue / Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 2\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 3\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 4\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 5\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 6\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 7\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/epilogue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 8\">Epilogue</a><hr />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Light_to_All\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Light to All\">Light to All</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/013-light/prologue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 9\">Prologue</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 10\">Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 11\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 12\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 13\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 14\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 15\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 16\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-8/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 17\">8</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-9/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 18\">9</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-10/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 19\">10</a> - <strong class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Epilogue Part 1</strong> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/epilogue-part-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 21\">Part 2</a><hr />\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/013-light/epilogue-part-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 21\">Next page</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" valign=\"top\">\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<caption><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Confessions_of_the_Creator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Confessions of the Creator\">Confessions of the Creator</a></b>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/000-creator/southern-areas/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 22\">Part 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/000-creator/shantotto-and-gabranth/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 23\">Part 2</a> - <a href=\"/story/000-creator/chasm-of-earth-and-flying-castle/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 24\">Part 3</a> - <a href=\"/story/000-creator/gaia-and-bahamut-isles/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 25\">Part 4</a> - <a href=\"/story/000-creator/land-of-discord-and-feral-chaos/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 26\">Part 5</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" valign=\"top\">\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<caption><b>Extras</b>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/reports/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Reports\">The Reports</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260901174416\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.065 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.087 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 3071/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 24991/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 7324/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 7/100\nExpensive parser function count: 2/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   25.110      1 -total\n 62.97%   15.812      7 Template:Map_D012\n 35.65%    8.952      1 Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Nav\n 22.55%    5.663      1 Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Nav2\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.9_prod_finalfantasy:pcache:idhash:156668-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timestamp 20260901174416 and revision id 3374494. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>";
